TASK B72
	TITLE "every subprocess leaves a structured record in the trail of its run, its tick or its"
		+ "command, and --verbose renders the records on stderr"
	STATUS todo
	MILESTONE @MILESTONE.F0
	COMPONENT "system"
	ROLE ada
	SPEC "ProcessRecord of brigade/system/run_process.py carries duration_ms, the integer"
		+ "milliseconds the subprocess took"
	SPEC "every subprocess brigade starts, through run_process or spawn_process, appends one line"
		+ "to the trail of the invocation that started it, whatever its exit code: a JSON document"
		+ "carrying schema_version 1, argv, cwd, exit, the exit code or null when there is none,"
		+ "duration_ms, null for a spawned run, outcome, one of exited, timed_out, not_found, cut"
		+ "for a client segment stopped by its wall limit and spawned for a run detached, and pid"
		+ "for a spawned run alone"
	SPEC "the trail of brigade run is runs/<id>/processes.jsonl, the client segment recorded after"
		+ "its wait and the records of a detached run written by the process it re-executes; the"
		+ "trail of a tick is $XDG_STATE_HOME/brigade/ticks/<instant>.jsonl, one file per tick,"
		+ "each round of tick --loop included; the trail of any other command is"
		+ "$XDG_STATE_HOME/brigade/commands/<instant>-<command>.jsonl; <instant> is the UTC compact"
		+ "form of the instant the command or the tick read"
	SPEC "at each tick and each command, the trails of ticks/ and commands/ older than trail_days"
		+ "of config.toml, 7 by default, are removed; a trail_days below 1 is an error naming the"
		+ "key and the file; the trail of a run is removed with its run"
	SPEC "--verbose is declared once on the common options next to --json and accepted by every"
		+ "subcommand; brigade <command> --verbose prints on stderr one line per record the command"
		+ "writes, \"brigade <command>: ran <argv joined by shlex.join>\" followed by \"exit <code>"
		+ "in <ms> ms\", \"timed out after <ms> ms\", \"not on PATH\", \"cut after <ms> ms\" or"
		+ "\"spawned pid <pid>\"; stdout carries the document alone, under --json too; without"
		+ "--verbose stderr carries no such line"
	SPEC "brigade run --detach --verbose prints the spawned line of the run, and the process it"
		+ "re-executes receives no --verbose"
	SPEC "tests/cli prove, through the fake adapter in a temporary state directory, the record of a"
		+ "subprocess whose exit code is refused in the trail of a run, the trail of a tick written"
		+ "and the trails older than trail_days removed, the trail of another command, and the"
		+ "--verbose lines on stderr with stdout unchanged"
	AFTER @TASK.B82
	RATIONALE "F2 of the foundations review: run_process.py:19-25 declares ProcessRecord with argv,"
		+ "cwd, exit code, stdout and stderr and no duration; cli.py:78-83 declares --json alone on"
		+ "the common options; 0 occurrences of verbose under brigade/; DESC 1 of"
		+ "@DECISION.OneRunnerForEverySubprocessAndGatewaysForGitAndAwawa reads \"exit code,"
		+ "stdout, stderr and duration\" and DESC 5 \"--verbose prints every subprocess argv, exit"
		+ "code and duration on stderr\"; plan section 4 line 253 and section 16 line 752"
		REF @DECISION.OneRunnerForEverySubprocessAndGatewaysForGitAndAwawa
	RATIONALE "the risk R4 of the review: without a trail a failing unattended tick leaves no"
		+ "subprocess record, the ledger run.finished carrying the client's duration_ms alone,"
		+ "run_segments.py:64; the trail of each tick answers it while the scheduler unit keeps"
		+ "running brigade tick --once without --verbose, brigade.service.tpl:7"
	RATIONALE "the user ruled to implement the decision rather than amend it, and that a trail is a"
		+ "structured record a brigade command reads, by"
		+ "@DECISION.EveryTraceIsAStructuredRecordThatABrigadeCommandReads: the records are always"
		+ "written to files, --verbose renders them for a person and nothing reads that rendering"
		+ "back; @TASK.B97 reads the trails"
		REF @DECISION.EveryTraceIsAStructuredRecordThatABrigadeCommandReads
